,{"title":"Child Process Node.js v5.7.0 Manual & Documentation","url":"https://nodejs.org/download/release/v5.7.0/docs/api/child_process.html"},{"title":"Child Process Node.js v6.2.1-rc.1 Manual & Documentation","url":"https://nodejs.org/download/rc/v6.2.1-rc.1/docs/api/child_process.html"},{"title":"Child Process","url":"https://nodejs.org/download/release/v6.8.0/docs/api/child_process.html"},{"title":"Child Process","url":"https://nodejs.org/download/release/v8.2.1/docs/api/child_process.html"},{"title":"Child Process","url":"https://nodejs.org/download/release/v8.6.0/docs/api/child_process.html"},{"title":"Child Process Node.js v4.0.0-rc.4 Manual & Documentation","url":"https://nodejs.org/download/rc/v4.0.0-rc.4/docs/api/child_process.html"},{"title":"Child Process Node.js v0.11.13 Manual & Documentation","url":"https://nodejs.org/docs/v0.11.13/api/child_process.html"},{"title":"Child Process","url":"https://nodejs.org/download/rc/v6.11.4-rc.2/docs/api/child_process.html"}]},"Based on the search results, here's what I found about Node.js `child_process.spawnSync`:\n\n## Overview\n\nThe child_process.spawnSync() function provides equivalent functionality in a synchronous manner that blocks the event loop until the spawned process either exits or is terminated.\n\n## Key Characteristics\n\nThe child_process.spawnSync(), child_process.execSync(), and child_process.execFileSync() methods are synchronous and will block the Node.js event loop, pausing execution of any additional code until the spawned process exits.\n\n## Syntax\n\nchild_process.spawnSync(command[, args][, options])\n\n## Return Value\n\nThe return object contains pid (Pid of the child process), output (Array of results from stdio output), and stdout/stderr (The contents of output[1] and output[2])\n\nThe official Node.js documentation can be found at: https://nodejs.org/api/child_process.html"],"durationSeconds":4.378796799999996,"searchCount":1},"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VAmngJmmxp81kprwvYmtKN","duration_ms":4379}}
